  id: spell-guiding-bolt
  displayName: Guiding Bolt
  description: A flash of light streaks toward a creature of your choice within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 4d6 radiant damage (treated as generic damage), and the next attack roll made against this target before the end of your next turn has advantage (not modeled -- no 'advantage until next turn' timer exists yet). When cast using a higher-level slot, damage increases by 1d6 per slot level above 1st.
